WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.000
The first star you will notice.

00:02.700 --> 00:06.433
As the sky darkens, the brightest stars come out first.

00:06.883 --> 00:12.315
A star twinkles because its light is a single point, pushed about by moving air.

00:12.765 --> 00:18.740
Its colour is its temperature: the bluish ones are hotter than the Sun, the orange ones cooler.
